Well, the thing is, reflection doesn't protect you from the effects of
those rays in the same ways it used to, and magic resistance doesn't
protect you from magical effects in the same ways it used to, either.
Touch of death, for example, does not instakill you.  When I played
(which was a year ago, but long enough for these changes to already
have been in place), I considered MR necessary but reflection not;
I honestly hadn't considered whether or not MC3 would be "necessary"
since it comes for free with any choice of reasonable cloak. (Yes,
displacement, I know, but it never seems to come up for me.) So the
"Play the game before you talk about what you need to win" still stands.

Specifically, http://sporkhack.com/older_changes.html look at the
changes for 7/11/07 and 7/15/07. You're welcome to disagree that all
aren't necessary (and you may be right, I'm not a spork expert) but you
might want to base your assertions on the game in question, rather than
the game it's based on that was written five years ago. I know Derek can
be pushy with this kind of thing, but in this case, he's right :)

