I'm inclined to prefer defense to offense as well, but there are a
couple of Spork-specific changes that make me consider the others if
I were ever to go back and ascend some more Sporkers. First, in Spork,
destroy armor gradually destroys your armor even through MR; I find this
about the most frustrating thing in the universe. It makes me wish I had
the mysterious force back. This means one of my main endgame priorities
is making the wizard _go away_ as quickly as possible. Orange or red
DSM may actually be best for this; I'm not sure.

Why red, you might say? It's also become much harder to hit high-level
monsters in Spork, especially but not only the Wizard, and so doing more
damage per successful hit means more successful hits. "Why not use a
wand of death like a normal person?" Also subject to to-hit code.

Having never played a game with most of the armor types, I think there are
a couple that merit consideration, and a couple that don't. Apparently
in my last win I tried Yellow Dragon Scale Mail successfully (I had to
go find the dump, http://sporkhack.com/dumps/raxohol.lastlog) so I guess
that's tenable? It was an ugly win, if I remember, though. I've never been
much good at Spork. :)

